=begin pod :kind("Type") :subkind("class") :category("basic")

=TITLE class RakuAST::Type::Enum

=SUBTITLE Represent a type without any additional features

    class RakuAST::Type::Enum { }

The C<RakuAST::Type::Enum> class represents an C<enum> specification.

=head2 Object introspection

C<RakuAST::Type::Enum> object is typically created when parsing
Raku Programming Language code.  So most developers will only need to
know how to introspect the objects created.

=head3 name

=begin code :preamble<my $enum>
say $enum.name;  # RakuAST::Name.from-identifier("Foo")
=end code

Returns the C<L<RakuAST::Name>|/type/RakuAST/Name> object of this
C<RakuAST::Type::Enum> object.

=head3 of

=begin code :preamble<my $enum>
say $enum.of;  # RakuAST::Type::Simple.from-identifier("Int")
=end code

Returns the C<RakuAST::Type>> object of this C<RakuAST::Type::Enum>
to which the C<enum> B<values> are constrained.

=head3 scope

=begin code :preamble<my $enum>
say $enum.scope;  # my
=end code

Returns the scope of the C<RakuAST::Type::Enum> object as a string.
Usually "our", but can also be "my" or "anon".

=head3 term

=begin code :preamble<my $enum>
dd $enum.term;  # <a b c>
=end code

Returns the L<C<RakuAST::Expression>|/Type/RakuAST/Expression> object
that represents the names and values of this C<enum>.

=head3 traits

=begin code :preamble<my $enum>
dd $enum.traits.head;  # of Str
=end code

Returns a (possibly empty) list of L<C<RakuAST::Trait>|/Type/RakuAST/Trait>
object that were applied to the C<enum>.

=head2 Object creation

There are is only one way to reate a C<RakuAST::Type::Enum> object.

=head3 new

=begin code
my $enum = RakuAST::Type::Enum.new(
  scope  => "my",
  name   => RakuAST::Name.from-identifier("Foo"),
  of     => RakuAST::Type::Simple.from-identifier("Int"),
  traits => (
    RakuAST::Trait::Of.new(
      RakuAST::Type::Simple.from-identifier("Str")
    ),
  ),
  term   => RakuAST::QuotedString.new(
    processors => <words val>,
    segments   => (
      RakuAST::StrLiteral.new("a b c"),
    )
  )
);
dd $enum;  # my Int enum Foo <a b c>
=end code

Creates a C<RakuAST::Type::Enum> object from the given named arguments.

=item scope - string indicating scope (my/our/anon), default: "our"
=item name - RakuAST::Name object with the name of the enum, default: ""
=item term - RakuAST::Expression with listing of keys/values (required)
=item traits - List of RakuAST::Trait objects, default: none
=item of - RakuAST::Type object constraining values, default: none

=end pod
